    "body": "Thank you for this report and the exact reproduction.\n\nTriage: `bug`, `P3` (wrong part size with no message; a workaround exists), `effort:high`, `area:2d`. The level is high because the fix decides when the program is refused or warned, and that is under the safety floor.\n\nWe agree with the direction of #1556 (Bore): the hole list of a Drill should name each hole the drill cannot make, by size. A pilot drill is a valid case, so a named warning that the user can accept is better than a silent skip.\n\nIf you want to work on it, comment a line that starts with `claimed:`. If not, our agents will pick it up in priority order.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
